\import{base-macros}

\p{The soundness review of the machine built hostile exports and found two families of accepts that the official checker and the reference engine reject: 9 exports under every switch set with \code{\verb~|probes~} (finding S-F1) and 3 under \code{\verb~|facts~} (S-F2). The cause is the same in both: the official definitional equality is not a congruence where a reduction inspects a proof. A recursor applied to a constructor reduces; applied to an opaque proof of the same proposition it is stuck; and the two arguments are equal by proof irrelevance. The shortcuts that compared arguments instead of unfolding, or skipped proof positions, were removed from both switches, which keep only their exact parts. The removed parts remain behind a system property, for measurement only. A test asserts the official verdict of the review's 29 conversion exports under every switch set of conversion.}

\p{Detail: [rep-soundness-machine](rep-soundness-machine), [rep-machine-M4](rep-machine-M4). Commit \commit{51fde1b}. Session: [the machine](ses-Z72N). Related: [the official relation is not a congruence](ins-4VH2), [the non-transitive triple](ex-OTWJ), [the proof-comparison shortcuts](design-proof-comparison-shortcuts).}
